---
import Container from '../components/ui/Container.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { resolveSiteHref } from '../lib/paths';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="Learn why RM Industries created Forge and how the project approaches generated source.">
  <Container size="md" class="pb-16">
    <article class="prose mx-auto">
      <div class="badge badge-outline">About Forge</div>
      <h1>A dependable beginning for content-driven websites.</h1>
      <p class="lead">RM Industries created Forge to connect content modeling, accessible presentation, CMS editing, quality checks, and deployment without taking ownership away from the people building the site.</p>

      <h2>Generated, then owned</h2>
      <p>Forge creates ordinary Astro source and a reproducible npm lockfile. There is no hosted runtime or hidden management layer: teams review, change, and deploy their project like any other repository.</p>

      <h2>Used by Forge itself</h2>
      <p>This project website was generated by the stable Forge package. It intentionally installs outside the Forge monorepo workspaces so the maintainers experience the same package boundaries as every other user.</p>

      <p>
        <a href={resolveSiteHref('/get-started/')}>Create a Forge site</a> or review the
        <a href={resolveSiteHref('/project/')}>project and support links</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </Container>
</BaseLayout>
